<worksheet >
    <title>IC-1 Double Integrals</title>
  <introduction>
    <p>To earn an M on this outcome, you will need to correctly complete all three problems. 
      To earn a P on this outcome, you will need to correctly complete problems 1 and 3 with progress on problem 2.</p>
  </introduction>  
  <page>
    <exercise workspace="2.5in"><p>Find the volume of the solid enclosed by the 
      paraboloid <m>z=x^2+4y^2</m> and the planes <m>z=0, x=0, y=3,</m> and <m>x=2y</m>.</p>
</exercise>
    <exercise>
        <introduction><p>The region, <m>R</m>, is bounded by the curves 
          <m>y=\ln(x), y=0</m>, and <m>x=e^2</m>.</p></introduction>
        <task><statement><p>Complete the integral that represents the volume 
          under the surface over the region. <md>\int_{\rule{2em}{0.1em}}^{\rule{2em}{0.1em}} \int_{\rule{2em}{0.1em}}^{\rule{2em}{0.1em}} \frac{1}{\ln(x)} dydx</md></p></statement></task>
        <task  workspace="2.0in"><statement><p>Evaluate the integral by reversing the order of integration.</p></statement></task>
    </exercise>
    </page>
    <page>
    <exercise workspace="1.5in">
        <p>Find the volume of the solid that lies under the paraboloid 
          <m>z=3(x^2+y^2)</m>, above the xy-plane, and inside the cylinder 
          <m>x^2+y^2=4y</m>.</p>
</exercise>
  </page>
</worksheet>